    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "name": "DHI-vtxe-6swf-5py2-mwxc",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2026-63349"
        ]
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:deb/dhi/airflow@3.3.0-0?distro=dhi-13"
        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:deb/dhi/airflow@3.3.0-1?distro=dhi-13"
        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:deb/dhi/airflow@3.3.0-2?distro=dhi-13"
        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:deb/dhi/airflow@3.3.0-3?distro=dhi-13"
        }
      ],
      "status": "affected",
      "action_statement": "Update airflow to 3.3.1-0 or later.",
      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-63349 (GHSA-3w57-8xmc-8v26): in AnyIO 4.14.0 and 4.14.1, open_process(), which run_process() also uses, passed the group argument to the backend in place of extra_groups, so a caller that set extra_groups=[] to drop inherited supplementary groups could start a child that kept the parent's groups. AnyIO 4.14.2 fixes it with https://github.com/agronholm/anyio/commit/eb562e6462ee46b1904e50b02ce00a858cdeb200, which passes extra_groups through in anyio/_core/_subprocesses.py (https://github.com/agronholm/anyio/security/advisories/GHSA-3w57-8xmc-8v26, https://github.com/agronholm/anyio/releases/tag/4.14.2). The airflow package bundles AnyIO in its Python environment under /usr/lib/airflow/lib/python3.13/site-packages, one copy per package. We read all 58 airflow packages for Debian 13 published in the DHI Debian repository by 2026-11-28, 3.3.0-0 to 3.4.0-17, amd64 and arm64 (116 package files). For every package we read its md5sums manifest, which lists every file the package installs with its digest, and matched the digests of the files that carry the fix against the same files in the released wheels on PyPI; we also unpacked the amd64 and arm64 packages of 3.3.0-0, 3.3.2-19, 3.4.0-0 and 3.4.0-17. Both architectures ship the same copy of those files in every version. 3.3.0-0 to 3.3.0-3 install AnyIO 4.14.1: their _subprocesses.py is byte for byte the file in the 4.14.1 wheel and sets kwargs['extra_groups'] = group. 3.3.1-0 to 3.3.1-15 install AnyIO 4.14.2, whose _subprocesses.py is byte for byte the 4.14.2 wheel's and sets kwargs['extra_groups'] = extra_groups. 3.3.2-0 to 3.3.2-19 (AnyIO 4.15.1) and 3.4.0-0 to 3.4.0-17 (AnyIO 4.16.0) all ship one further digest of the file, and the unpacked 3.3.2-19 and 3.4.0-17 copies pass extra_groups too. 3.3.1-0 is the first published package with the fix."
    },
